{%- comment -%}
  Wig Party — MOBILE DRAWER NAVIGATION (below 1280px).

  A different interaction pattern over the same content, not a shrunken mega menu. Desktop
  is hover + a full-bleed panel of columns; this is tap + a nested drawer that drills down
  one level at a time.

  STRUCTURE

    .aria-mnav                     fixed, full-viewport, holds the overlay and the drawer
      .aria-mnav__overlay          backdrop; tapping it closes everything
      .aria-mnav__drawer           the sliding panel — role="dialog" aria-modal="true"
        .aria-mnav__level--root    LEVEL 1: the main menu list
        .aria-mnav__level--child   LEVEL 2: one per parent that owns a mega menu

  DRILL-DOWN, NOT ACCORDION. Each level is its own absolutely-positioned layer filling the
  drawer. Level 2 sits off-canvas at translateX(100%) and slides over level 1 when opened,
  so the previous level is REPLACED rather than pushed down. Nothing expands underneath a
  parent. `assets/aria-mobile-nav.js` drives the state; CSS owns the motion.

  BACK vs CLOSE are deliberately different controls with different jobs:
    Back  (level 2 only)  returns to level 1 and never closes the drawer
    Close (both levels)   closes the whole drawer from wherever you are

  CONTENT COMES FROM THE MEGA MENU BLOCKS. Level 2 renders `aria-mega-menu` with
  `context: 'mobile'`, so the columns, menus, headings, icons, feature cards, promo cards,
  photo rows and media cards are the same definitions the desktop panel uses — one source,
  two presentations. Product cards are the single exception and are skipped in
  `aria-mega-column` (see the note there). Nothing about the menu content is restated here.

  A parent with no mega block stays a plain link, exactly as it does in the desktop header.

  Params:
    section       (required) the header section, for its blocks and settings
    menu          (required) the main_menu link_list
    mega_names    (required) '~'-joined parent labels that own a panel  } built once in
    mega_ids      (required) '~'-joined block ids, parallel to the above } header.liquid
    placeholders  (optional) pass through the placeholder-rows switch
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- liquid
  assign mnav_id = 'AriaMnav-' | append: section.id
  assign name_list = mega_names | split: '~'
  assign id_list = mega_ids | split: '~'
-%}

<div class="aria-mnav" id="{{ mnav_id }}" data-aria-mnav hidden>
  {%- comment -%}
    The overlay is a sibling of the drawer, not a parent, so the drawer is never inside a
    fading element — animating the backdrop's opacity would otherwise take the drawer's
    contents with it.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  <div class="aria-mnav__overlay" data-mnav-close tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"></div>

  <div
    class="aria-mnav__drawer"
    role="dialog"
    aria-modal="true"
    aria-label="{{ 'aria_theme.header.primary_nav' | t }}"
    data-mnav-drawer
  >
    {%- comment -%} ---------- LEVEL 1: the main menu ---------- {%- endcomment -%}
    <div class="aria-mnav__level aria-mnav__level--root is-active" data-mnav-level="root">
      <div class="aria-mnav__head">
        <span class="aria-mnav__title">{{ 'aria_theme.header.menu_title' | t }}</span>
        <button
          type="button"
          class="aria-mnav__icon-btn aria-mnav__close"
          data-mnav-close
        >
          {%- render 'aria-icon', name: 'close' -%}
          <span class="visually-hidden">{{ 'aria_theme.header.close_menu' | t }}</span>
        </button>
      </div>

      <div class="aria-mnav__body">
        <ul class="aria-mnav__list" role="list">
          {%- for link in menu.links -%}
            {%- liquid
              comment
                Same lookup the desktop nav loop uses, against the same two parallel lists,
                so a parent owns a drawer panel on exactly the same condition that it owns
                a mega panel.
              endcomment
              assign has_panel = false
              assign panel_block_id = ''
              for mega_name in name_list
                if mega_name == link.title
                  assign has_panel = true
                  assign panel_block_id = id_list[forloop.index0]
                  break
                endif
              endfor

              assign show_dot = false
              if section.settings.show_live_dot and section.settings.live_dot_menu_item != blank and link.title == section.settings.live_dot_menu_item
                assign show_dot = true
              endif
            -%}

            <li class="aria-mnav__item">
              {%- if has_panel -%}
                {%- comment -%}
                  A real <button>: it opens a panel rather than navigating, and the parent's
                  own URL stays reachable from the "View all" link at the foot of level 2.
                {%- endcomment -%}
                <button
                  type="button"
                  class="aria-mnav__link aria-mnav__link--parent"
                  data-mnav-open="{{ mnav_id }}-{{ panel_block_id }}"
                >
                  <span class="aria-mnav__link-label">
                    {{ link.title }}
                    {%- if show_dot -%}
                      <span class="aria-header__live-dot aria-live-pulse" aria-hidden="true"></span>
                      <span class="visually-hidden">{{ 'aria_theme.header.live_now' | t }}</span>
                    {%- endif -%}
                  </span>
                  {%- render 'aria-icon', name: 'arrow-right', class: 'aria-mnav__chevron' -%}
                </button>
              {%- elsif link.links.size > 0 -%}
                {%- comment -%}
                  A plain Shopify parent with children and no mega block: it drills down
                  too, into a generated level-2 list, so the drawer has ONE interaction
                  model rather than an accordion for some items and a drill-down for
                  others. (The store's `navigation` menu is currently flat, so this branch
                  is a robustness path, not the common case.)
                {%- endcomment -%}
                <button
                  type="button"
                  class="aria-mnav__link aria-mnav__link--parent"
                  data-mnav-open="{{ mnav_id }}-sub-{{ forloop.index }}"
                >
                  <span class="aria-mnav__link-label">{{ link.title }}</span>
                  {%- render 'aria-icon', name: 'arrow-right', class: 'aria-mnav__chevron' -%}
                </button>
              {%- else -%}
                <a
                  href="{{ link.url }}"
                  class="aria-mnav__link"
                  {% if link.active %}aria-current="page"{% endif %}
                >
                  <span class="aria-mnav__link-label">
                    {{ link.title }}
                    {%- if show_dot -%}
                      <span class="aria-header__live-dot aria-live-pulse" aria-hidden="true"></span>
                      <span class="visually-hidden">{{ 'aria_theme.header.live_now' | t }}</span>
                    {%- endif -%}
                  </span>
                </a>
              {%- endif -%}
            </li>
          {%- endfor -%}
        </ul>

        {%- comment -%}
          NO account/cart buttons here. An earlier version repeated them at the foot of the
          drawer, but both already sit in the mobile header row itself and stay reachable
          while the drawer is open, so the pair was duplicate navigation. The drawer holds
          menu content only.
        {%- endcomment -%}
      </div>
    </div>

    {%- comment -%} ---------- LEVEL 2: one panel per mega parent ---------- {%- endcomment -%}
    {%- for link in menu.links -%}
      {%- liquid
        assign has_panel = false
        assign panel_block_id = ''
        for mega_name in name_list
          if mega_name == link.title
            assign has_panel = true
            assign panel_block_id = id_list[forloop.index0]
            break
          endif
        endfor
      -%}

      {%- if has_panel -%}
        <div
          class="aria-mnav__level aria-mnav__level--child"
          id="{{ mnav_id }}-{{ panel_block_id }}"
          data-mnav-level="child"
          hidden
        >
          <div class="aria-mnav__head">
            <button type="button" class="aria-mnav__icon-btn aria-mnav__back" data-mnav-back>
              {%- render 'aria-icon', name: 'arrow-left' -%}
              <span class="visually-hidden">{{ 'aria_theme.header.back' | t }}</span>
            </button>
            <span class="aria-mnav__title">{{ link.title }}</span>
            <button type="button" class="aria-mnav__icon-btn aria-mnav__close" data-mnav-close>
              {%- render 'aria-icon', name: 'close' -%}
              <span class="visually-hidden">{{ 'aria_theme.header.close_menu' | t }}</span>
            </button>
          </div>

          <div class="aria-mnav__body">
            {%- comment -%}
              THE SHARED CONTENT. Same snippet, same block, same branch as desktop — only
              `context` differs. Product cards drop out inside `aria-mega-column`; the
              feature cards, promo cards, photo rows, media card and every menu column
              stay, and go responsive via component-aria-mobile-nav.css.
            {%- endcomment -%}
            {%- for mega in section.blocks -%}
              {%- if mega.id == panel_block_id -%}
                {%- render 'aria-mega-menu',
                  block: mega,
                  id: mnav_id,
                  context: 'mobile',
                  placeholders: placeholders
                -%}
              {%- endif -%}
            {%- endfor -%}

            {%- comment -%}
              The parent's own destination. The level-1 row is a <button> that opens this
              panel, so without this the parent link itself would be unreachable on mobile.
              Not for the header's menu-only parents (Start Here), which have no page.
            {%- endcomment -%}
            {%- liquid
              assign menu_only = false
              assign menu_only_list = section.settings.menu_only_items | split: ','
              for menu_only_raw in menu_only_list
                assign menu_only_name = menu_only_raw | strip
                if menu_only_name == link.title
                  assign menu_only = true
                  break
                endif
              endfor
            -%}
            {%- if link.url != blank and link.url != '#' and menu_only == false -%}
              <a href="{{ link.url }}" class="aria-mnav__viewall">
                {{ 'aria_theme.header.view_all' | t }}
                {{ link.title }}
              </a>
            {%- endif -%}
          </div>
        </div>
      {%- elsif link.links.size > 0 -%}
        <div
          class="aria-mnav__level aria-mnav__level--child"
          id="{{ mnav_id }}-sub-{{ forloop.index }}"
          data-mnav-level="child"
          hidden
        >
          <div class="aria-mnav__head">
            <button type="button" class="aria-mnav__icon-btn aria-mnav__back" data-mnav-back>
              {%- render 'aria-icon', name: 'arrow-left' -%}
              <span class="visually-hidden">{{ 'aria_theme.header.back' | t }}</span>
            </button>
            <span class="aria-mnav__title">{{ link.title }}</span>
            <button type="button" class="aria-mnav__icon-btn aria-mnav__close" data-mnav-close>
              {%- render 'aria-icon', name: 'close' -%}
              <span class="visually-hidden">{{ 'aria_theme.header.close_menu' | t }}</span>
            </button>
          </div>
          <div class="aria-mnav__body">
            <ul class="aria-mnav__list" role="list">
              {%- for childlink in link.links -%}
                <li class="aria-mnav__item">
                  <a
                    href="{{ childlink.url }}"
                    class="aria-mnav__link"
                    {% if childlink.active %}aria-current="page"{% endif %}
                  >
                    <span class="aria-mnav__link-label">{{ childlink.title }}</span>
                  </a>
                </li>
              {%- endfor -%}
            </ul>
            {%- if link.url != blank and link.url != '#' -%}
              <a href="{{ link.url }}" class="aria-mnav__viewall">
                {{ 'aria_theme.header.view_all' | t }}
                {{ link.title }}
              </a>
            {%- endif -%}
          </div>
        </div>
      {%- endif -%}
    {%- endfor -%}
  </div>
</div>
